  "data/ingredients/unmapped/3-methylacetate.yaml": {
    "raw_text": "identifier: UNMAPPED_0736\npreferred_term: 3-methylacetate\nsynonyms:\n- synonym_text: 3-methylacetate\n  synonym_type: RAW_TEXT\n  source: microbedecoder\nmapping_status: REJECTED\noccurrence_statistics:\n  total_occurrences: 0\n  media_count: 0\n  source_occurrences:\n  - source: microbedecoder\n    count: 1\n    source_columns: bergey:minor_end_products\ncuration_history:\n- timestamp: '2026-08-04T02:54:09.684805+00:00'\n  curator: audit_import_ingredients[microbedecoder]\n  action: CREATED_AS_UNMAPPED\n  changes: Imported from microbedecoder (source_id=kgmicrobe.compound:3_methylacetate);\n    no CAS-RN or CHEBI/NCIT match. Curator review needed.\n  new_status: UNMAPPED\n  llm_assisted: false\n- timestamp: '2026-08-06T00:00:00+00:00'\n  curator: issue_213_residual_triage\n  action: FLAGGED_NEEDS_EXPERT\n  changes: 'Parse fragment: acetate has no position 3, so this is a truncation of\n    a longer name. Searched CHEBI, NCIT, FOODON, ENVO, MeSH, BTO and UBERON by label\n    and synonym with normalisation, plus exact queries across all of live OLS4.'\n  previous_status: UNMAPPED\n  new_status: NEEDS_EXPERT\n  llm_assisted: true\n- timestamp: '2026-08-06T00:00:00+00:00'\n  curator: edison_literature_identity\n  action: ANNOTATED\n  changes: 'Edison LITERATURE (PaperQA3) identity research; report at research/ingredients/3-methylacetate-edison-literature.md\n    (local artifact \u2014 research/ is gitignored, so the findings are quoted here rather\n    than linked). Report verdict: ## Executive recommendation \u2014 **Retain `UNMAPPED`.\n    Do not create an SSSOM row.** The string `3-methylacetate` is not adequately specified\n    as a chemical name, salt, hydrate, mixture, buffer, or named formulation. No retrieved\n    source establishes it as a standalone culture-medium ingredient. No ontology CURIE\n    was proposed. Recorded as provenance only \u2014 no grounding applied from this run.\n    Edison''s recommendations are deliberately conservative, and a plausible identifier\n    promoted by a mechanism that never decided anything is what #203 and #263 exist\n    to undo. Any CURIE above is a curator''s to accept or reject.'\n  llm_assisted: true\n- timestamp: '2026-08-15T00:00:00+00:00'\n  curator: retire_assay_labels\n  action: RETIRED_NOT_AN_INGREDIENT\n  previous_status: NEEDS_EXPERT\n  new_status: REJECTED\n  changes: 'Retired as an ingredient record (#213/#308): not a chemical name and not\n    reconstructable. It is a fragment from the same importer that produced `Formate+3-methyl\n    Mercaptopropionate`, so the likely original is `3-methyl mercaptopropionate` \u2014\n    but its partner text is absent from the corpus, and guessing it would invent a\n    compound. Not mapped, because every substrate CURIE it could be grounded to is\n    already the primary key of a live record \u2014 in MIM the identifier IS the ontology\n    CURIE, so a mapping here would mint a duplicate rather than add coverage. No synonym\n    is folded onto those records either: this label names a reaction or a splice,\n    not the substance, and asserting the synonymy would make label_index resolve it\n    to something it does not denote.'\n  llm_assisted: false\n- timestamp: '2026-11-08T02:36:20.627642+00:00'\n  curator: claude\n  action: CORRECTED_SOURCE_PROVENANCE\n  changes: 'Correct active source-origin notes only (#1151): raw database.csv SHA256=0c6ff730a108720a5d6972400f2bccf2eca8621713b62736abdf5df0fb188c95,\n    record19685 canonical SHA256=f96206bc73f8fa93d7a144e6f4f586e8e464d23b31d8093a0d510bc5d272302a,\n    contains 3-methylacetate in original prose and structured minor-product field.\n    Retain unresolved identity, REJECTED status, all raw synonyms, counts and prior\n    history; add no ontology mapping, replacement identity, role or release approval.\n    The original primary paper was not independently re-read in this provenance check.'\n  previous_status: REJECTED\n  new_status: REJECTED\n  llm_assisted: true\nnotes: 'Imported from MicrobeDecoder (source_id=kgmicrobe.compound:3_methylacetate).\n  The literal 3-methylacetate is present in both the raw Bergey_Text_for_end_products\n  and Bergey_Minor_end_products fields for Telmatobacter bradus, LPSN 789679, database.csv\n  record 19685 (source citation https://doi.org/10.1002/9781118960608.gbm01426). This\n  is reported minor-product provenance, not an established chemical identity or growth-medium\n  ingredient. The prior importer-fragment explanation and proposed 3-methyl mercaptopropionate\n  reconstruction are unsupported by this source and are superseded; their original\n  wording remains in curation history and the archived preimage. Retain REJECTED status\n  and no ontology mapping until identity and ingredient/product scope are resolved.\n  No replacement compound is inferred. Evidence and exact source hashes: reports/kgm_unmapped_chemicals_20261107/methylacetate/sources/manifest.json;\n  issue #1151.'\n",
